#
# Counter-example for math:RationalValueShape: a math:RationalValue whose
# math:denominator is 0. p/0 is not a rational value, so the exact carrier is
# ill-formed. The numerator is present and both are integers. The generated
# views include shacl.NotConstraintComponent and the constraint's derived
# shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent, attributed to math:ZeroDenominator.
# The conformance cell selects failure-class isolation; its declared component
# and source-shape fields add no further pin in that execution branch.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecRationalValueZeroDenominator).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:zeroDenomRational a math:RationalValue ;
    math:numerator 1 ;
    math:denominator 0 .
